 "title": "Arena: a telegraphed heavy blow",
 "about": "A stranger with a spear walks up to the subject and, every time, opens with its slowest, heaviest blow (`attack` with a spear: a 750 ms windup the target can see, 9 damage), then stands for 2 or 3 s before the next (mending its own wounds first when below 70 health, with the ordinary `heal` and the `wound_tending` it is given, so it lasts the fight; no armor). When it has been more than 5 m from the subject for 4 s (night sight is 6 m; a pause is at most 3 s), it walks to where the subject stands and fights again: `attack` closes in only on someone it sees. The pattern a person learns: step out of reach or dodge during the windup, and strike in the pause. The opponent is a trial fixture (a resident whose graph the trial sets; docs/COMBAT_MIND.md \u00a74.1), never game content: nothing here is installed into any character, and the subject's mind is told nothing about it. Subject: a spawned newcomer on its own instinct graph, its mind the only one thinking; the newcomer's kit plus a spear. A world hour is 30 real seconds; the world starts at 10:00 (day sight).",
